WEBVTT

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.840
You're those boys from the other day!

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:06.880
Sorry for bothering you then.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.410
Why did you show up here again?

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:11.490
Are you here to apologize 
for making Zenko cry?

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.200
W-Wait a minute!

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.710
We're here because Zenko called us!

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:16.700
She called you?

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.880
I'll delete her number right now!

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:20.240
Don't delete it.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.650
Sorry for asking you to 
come on such short notice.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:24.620
Come in.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.220
Excuse the intrusion.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:29.750
Zenko, you're letting them in here?

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.630
Dad, if you keep being rude to my friends,

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:37.010
I'll tell Mom everything.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.830
How's Yahiko?

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:42.020
Well, he's full of energy.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:48.150
Haruitsuki, help.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.420
I'm stuck and can't get out.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:26.920
When I got home from 
school, he was like this.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:31.380
<b>Mystery 10 "The Fool"</b>

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:30.800
A lot of yokai grow when they feel distressed.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.280
I'm not distressed.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:34.430
I even had yummy rakugan as a snack.

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:38.440
I took a nap in the sun, and 
when I woke up, I was like this.

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:40.260
And I can't get back to normal.

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:42.760
Did you do anything before your nap?

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.010
Like what?

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.260
Like scavenging for food?

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:46.890
Don't make fun of me!

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:48.940
I don't scavenge for food!

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:51.480
I've only eaten rakugan and potatoes today!

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:53.000
Potatoes?

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:59.150
I didn't scavenge them. I snitched them.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:00.640
Don't act like that's any better.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.490
That's even worse!

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.470
Is this what you snitched, Yahiko?

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.290
Fuzzy is here?

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.610
I didn't notice, since he's semi-transparent.

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:14.380
He's semi-transparent to you?

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:18.880
I can see Yahiko clearly,
but I can't see Fuzzy very well.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:21.510
Yeah. This is definitely the smell.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:26.390
My dad apparently had them for 
lunch, but he's feeling fine.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:30.580
These smell kind of weird...

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:31.770
Th-They stink!

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.400
They smell so acrid!

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.240
It doesn't bother you, Zenko?

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:36.810
Do they smell that bad?

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:38.750
Ah, that smells great.

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.910
I wish I could eat just one more.

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:41.860
No.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.630
Hey, Haruitsuki.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.070
I didn't notice before,

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:53.500
but these smell faintly of yokai.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.390
I smell it in the dirt on the potatoes.

00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:58.640
The dirt?

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:03.120
My mom borrowed part of a parishioner's 
farm and grew them there.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:06.700
Then the cause might be at the farm 
where these were grown, right,

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:07.770
Abeno-san?

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:10.640
Close that bag first, would you?

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:14.320
I'm not letting you go out with those boys.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.350
If you insist on going, then I'll—

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:17.870
Don't follow us.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:19.360
We're just going to the farm.

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:24.610
I think maybe your dad hates us.

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:27.620
He probably sees us as pests 
clinging to his daughter.

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:32.370
Sorry, guys.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:36.600
Not only am I causing 
you trouble over Yahiko,

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:39.270
but my dad's being a jerk to you, too.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:44.480
But isn't he acting that way 
because he's worried about you?

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:46.630
I think he's a good father.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:47.930
Now, let's go.

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:51.930
Besides, you're not bothering us 
by asking us to help Yahiko.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:56.420
If anything, I'm sorry Yahiko 
seems to be causing you trouble.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.190
We'll do our best to take care of it.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.590
The way you talk is so formal.

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:01.700
Are we really the same age?

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.210
Don't measure me by your 
five-year-old standards.

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:04.990
You're treating me like I'm five again!

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:07.320
I definitely act my age more than you do!

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:06.810
<i>I'm glad.</i>

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:08.600
What? How?

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:09.960
Stop fighting.

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:11.620
Okay.

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:11.620
Okay.

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:16.710
<i>I hope my dad grows to like them soon, too.</i>

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:20.470
Is this the farm?

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:20.960
Yeah.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:23.080
I-It stinks...

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:27.180
Does this not bother the neighbors?

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:31.720
We're probably the only ones 
who see the farm this way.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:34.180
Just us? Which means...

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:37.190
Yeah. I sense a yokai in there.

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:39.240
Then we should go in and look for—

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:43.960
Can you make it, Abeno-san?

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:44.990
Don't worry about it.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:46.590
I just won't breathe.

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:49.000
That'll kill you!

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:52.920
Fine, then. I can tolerate 
the smell better than you.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:54.360
You can count on me.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:55.830
<i>I don't want to!</i>

00:05:57.940 --> 00:05:58.940
Hanae...

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:00.080
What?

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:02.920
Fuzzy! When did he get there?

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:04.030
Your fur! Your fur!

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.110
Your beautiful fur!

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:08.090
You're covered in mud.

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:09.720
I'll have to wash you later.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:11.390
Hey, Hanae...

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:13.620
Has Fuzzy gotten bigger?

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.470
H-He's heavy!

00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:26.150
Looks like we can be certain that
Yahiko grew because of this mud, too.

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:28.400
How can we make him go 
back to the way he was?

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:31.300
Hairball and Zenko, you wait here.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:31.910
Okay.

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:33.710
Let's go, Ashiya.

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:34.410
Okay.

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:41.140
It stinks!

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:43.710
Shut up!

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:46.460
But it stinks way more than it did outside!

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:52.730
<i>Just the stench is distracting enough...</i>

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:55.660
Abeno-san?

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:10.780
He's hitting his face?

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:11.690
It hurts!

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:13.660
Stop that!

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:16.430
Don't beat your head with a rock! 
Are you trying to kill yourself?

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:17.840
Boy!

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.410
Don't be hasty!

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:23.340
My, my. Please, you're 
jumping to conclusions.

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:24.780
That's not a rock.

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:25.980
A potato.

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:27.840
Huh? A potato?

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.040
I got it from this farm.

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:31.530
Well, it's confusing!

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:33.800
Oh, dear. I've been scolded.

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:35.800
But more importantly...

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:39.180
It's been so long since I last spoke to someone.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:41.190
And it's my first time talking to humans.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:44.540
Please call me Nobou.

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:47.320
By the way, who are you boys?

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:50.800
I'm Abeno, master of the Mononokean.

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:52.200
I'm his employee, Ashiya.

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:55.720
The Mononokean?! You mean the rumored...

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:56.460
Rumored?

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:58.380
You're the yokai kidnappers

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:02.030
who entice yokai one after another 
and take them to the Underworld!

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:05.000
No, we're exorcists.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.210
But depending on your perspective,

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:09.200
that's not entirely wrong.

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:10.590
So you do kidnap them.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.720
We're not kidnapping anybody!

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:17.510
I hope they're okay.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:22.980
<b>The Morose Mononokean</b>

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:27.320
I see. So that's how you kidnap yokai 
and take them to the Underworld.

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:29.290
Not "kidnap"! We exorcise them!

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:31.820
As far as I'm concerned, whether 
you kidnap or exorcise me,

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:34.250
I don't care what you do, as long 
as I can get away from here.

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:38.170
Abeno-dono, Ashiya-dono, 
I cannot leave this place.

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:41.190
I'd like you to help me 
escape to the Underworld!

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:42.500
Oh, my.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.000
It stinks!

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:47.020
Nobou-dono, do you know what this mud is?

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:51.310
This mud welled up from the ground one day.

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:54.640
When I walk through the mud 
to try and leave this place,

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:58.480
I start to feel more and more depressed.

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:01.350
Eventually, I can't move.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:01.350
Nobou-san!

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:06.510
Then I'm enveloped in this 
smoke and see a phantasmagoria,

00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:09.930
and end up coming back here.

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:10.860
A phantasmagoria?

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:13.880
So in order to stop seeing 
the phantasmagoria,

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:16.190
I thought I'd hit my head 
and erase my memories.

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:18.350
That's why you were beating 
your head with a potato?

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:22.370
Having tried everything,
I was about to give up hope.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:25.480
But if you send me to the Underworld,

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:28.380
then I'll finally be able to leave this place.

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:30.220
Come, Mononokean!

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:32.380
Send me to the Underworld right away!

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:34.130
I can't exorcise you.

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:36.150
I'm sorry.

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:36.980
Oh, my.

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:38.970
My, my, my...

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:39.890
Abeno-san?

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:42.260
The smell's bothering me so much,

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:45.150
I can't focus on summoning 
a portal to the Underworld.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:49.470
We'll get you out of this field,

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:53.230
then I'll send you to the 
Underworld. Is that all right?

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:56.440
But when I walk through the mud...

00:09:56.440 --> 00:09:57.700
Yes, so...

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:58.960
Heave-ho.

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:02.790
You seem to be fine when 
you're not touching the mud.

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:06.430
Okay, here we go.

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:08.060
Thank you.

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:16.630
We're still not out of the smoke?

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:19.680
That's odd. It shouldn't be this far.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:22.760
<i>I'm having trouble focusing 
because of the smell.</i>

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:27.020
<i>But on top of that, this 
smoke keeps getting thicker.</i>

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:27.770
Abeno-san?

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:32.520
I was using the hairball's 
presence to navigate,

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:33.960
but I've completely lost him.

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:36.530
What?! Are we stuck in here, too?

00:10:36.980 --> 00:10:38.030
<i>I have no choice.</i>

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:42.670
Nobou-dono, I'll try exorcising you here.

00:10:42.670 --> 00:10:46.540
Here? Oh, I'm starting to feel nervous.

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:48.600
Can you summon a portal here?

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:51.200
But isn't the smell even stronger here?

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:55.370
We should at least go where 
there's less smoke...

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:56.210
Ashiya.

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:56.990
Huh?

00:10:57.440 --> 00:10:59.710
For just thirty seconds, shut up.

00:10:59.710 --> 00:11:01.140
Sorry.

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:03.480
<i>Thirty seconds, huh?</i>

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:10.150
<i>Abeno-san is going to be mad!</i>

00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:14.730
I'm sorry, Abeno-san!

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:16.680
Huh? A scarecrow?

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:25.180
Where am I?

00:11:25.180 --> 00:11:29.820
Did you see how hard
I just worked, my friend?

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:30.870
Nobou-san!

00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:34.660
Sorry. Did I let go of you at some point?

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:41.930
Wasn't I impressive, my friend?

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:42.510
<i>Is this...</i>

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:45.510
You just praised me, didn't you?

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:47.510
Thank you.

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:48.520
<i>Nobou-san's phantasmagoria?</i>

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:51.450
But you, my friend, are even 
more splendid than I am.

00:11:51.450 --> 00:11:54.490
I am so fortunate because you always listen

00:11:53.590 --> 00:11:55.990
Nobou-san, hello?

00:11:54.490 --> 00:11:56.330
to everything I have to say.

00:11:56.330 --> 00:12:00.120
And I enjoy protecting the rice together, too.

00:12:02.690 --> 00:12:06.490
What came next happened 
in the blink of an eye.

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:10.000
I tried to carry my friend to safety,

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:14.650
but it was so hot, and I was so terrified.

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:20.990
When I see this memory, this phantasmagoria,

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:25.040
I return once again to this place.

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:28.900
It's as though my friend is 
stopping me from leaving.

00:12:28.900 --> 00:12:32.430
It's as though my friend 
resents me for being unable

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:34.270
to save him that day.

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:36.270
Nobou-san...

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:38.270
Nobou-dono...

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:43.000
With your help, I thought I 
could finally leave this place.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:45.430
Or so I believed,

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:48.780
but my friend must resent me.

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:53.290
Unwilling to forgive me for simply 
standing there instead of saving him,

00:12:53.670 --> 00:12:58.230
he has bound me here so 
I can't leave this place.

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:01.600
You're wrong.

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:03.920
You were trying to save him.

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:05.550
That wasn't your fault!

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:07.850
Ashiya-dono...

00:13:09.380 --> 00:13:11.320
But I—

00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:13.810
I believe it's your fault.

00:13:15.030 --> 00:13:15.940
Abeno-san?

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:20.390
Nobou-dono, in your current state,

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:23.240
you cannot leave this place.

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:26.820
I can't exorcise you.

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:29.930
I see.

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:32.830
Then it can't be helped.

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:36.910
Abeno-san, didn't you 
see that phantasmagoria?

00:13:36.910 --> 00:13:37.690
I did.

00:13:37.690 --> 00:13:40.970
Then if you think that was Nobou-san's fault,

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:43.390
what did he do wrong?

00:13:43.390 --> 00:13:45.170
I don't think it was Nobou-san's fault.

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:46.380
Ow!

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:50.640
What if that had been you?

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:51.890
Huh?

00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:54.700
If you saw someone you cared about burning,

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:56.900
and all you could do was watch,

00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:59.690
could you really claim you're not responsible?

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:01.850
Nobou-dono,

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:06.950
it's not your friend binding you here.

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:09.930
You're doing this to yourself.

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:11.910
What? I am?

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:16.090
Don't you think it's possible you 
subconsciously created this mud and smoke

00:14:16.090 --> 00:14:20.760
to trap yourself so you couldn't 
run from your friend again,

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:22.420
like you did that day?

00:14:29.780 --> 00:14:32.860
Oh, my. What is this?

00:14:32.860 --> 00:14:35.930
I'm crying...

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:41.100
I can't forcibly exorcise you 
when you don't want to leave,

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:46.070
but you can't stay here any longer.

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:50.570
Nobou-dono, you must 
resolve yourself to leave.

00:14:51.170 --> 00:14:53.580
Resolve myself to leave?

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:58.250
Ashiya, we're going back 
to the hairball and Zenko.

00:14:58.250 --> 00:14:59.580
What about Nobou-san?

00:14:59.930 --> 00:15:02.980
Nobou-dono will have to 
leave this place on his own.

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:06.670
That won't change anything!

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:09.090
Nobou-san can't leave by himself.

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:11.750
You can drag yourself along the ground.

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:15.100
As long as you keep moving through the smoke,

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:18.100
you can escape this place.

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:24.220
It's from Zenko.

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:26.040
She says, "Are you okay?"

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:28.360
Tell her we're on our way back.

00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:30.060
Got it.

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:32.920
Nobou-dono, take all the time you need.

00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:34.200
Follow us.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:37.550
But if the mud and smoke beat me,

00:15:37.550 --> 00:15:40.240
and I can't leave on my own...

00:15:40.240 --> 00:15:41.460
We'll wait.

00:15:40.240 --> 00:15:41.460
We'll wait.

00:15:43.910 --> 00:15:47.560
In any case, I'm not going to abandon you.

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:48.750
Let's go, Ashiya.

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:51.590
Wait...

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:54.390
Please wait!

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:58.200
You may be waiting for me forever.

00:15:58.200 --> 00:15:58.890
Yet...

00:15:59.300 --> 00:16:02.640
Yet will you still wait for me?

00:16:03.320 --> 00:16:04.060
Yes.

00:16:03.320 --> 00:16:04.060
Yes.

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:08.440
See you later.

00:16:09.590 --> 00:16:11.740
Ugh, this stinks. I forgot.

00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:22.140
My friend, by shackling 
myself with mud and smoke,

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:25.300
perhaps I believed thinking 
of you for an eternity

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:27.770
would allow me to atone for what I did.

00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:28.920
But...

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:33.800
My friend, I am leaving this place.

00:16:37.110 --> 00:16:40.630
This time, I won't be coming back.

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:58.360
<i>I must move forward,</i>

00:16:58.360 --> 00:17:02.330
<i>for those two who said 
they would wait for me.</i>

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:08.330
<i>This will probably be the last time we meet,</i>

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:12.840
<i>so there is something I must tell you.</i>

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:21.980
My friend, if I had endured
the heat of the flames

00:17:21.980 --> 00:17:26.230
for just a bit longer, and pulled harder...

00:17:27.330 --> 00:17:30.890
If I'd noticed the fire a little sooner,

00:17:30.890 --> 00:17:33.260
I might have been able to save you.

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:35.440
I am sorry, my friend.

00:17:35.440 --> 00:17:37.670
I'm sorry I couldn't save you.

00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:43.680
But because I ran that day, I met them.

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:48.560
And for the first time, I felt 
glad that I ran that day.

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:50.750
Because I felt that way,

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:57.530
I believe it is presumptuous
of me to call you my friend.

00:17:57.530 --> 00:18:01.920
But still, my friend,

00:18:01.920 --> 00:18:05.020
the days I spent with you 
were absolutely delightful.

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:08.250
All my memories of them are wonderful.

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:11.770
There is no happiness like it.

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:17.350
My friend, thank you for being my friend.

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:20.360
Truly, thank you.

00:18:31.760 --> 00:18:36.510
<i>Goodbye, my friend.</i>

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:41.190
<i>Goodbye.</i>

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:49.700
Nobou-san still isn't here.

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:54.570
Is Abeno asleep?

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:57.320
He said not to talk to him 
because he's focusing.

00:18:57.320 --> 00:18:59.500
Focusing? On what?

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:02.060
Summoning an Underworld portal.

00:19:02.060 --> 00:19:03.580
Apparently the smell bothers him.

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:05.580
<i>An Underworld portal?</i>

00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:08.000
Zenko, you can go home.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:09.580
Your dad must be worried.

00:19:10.150 --> 00:19:11.110
No, it's okay.

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:14.120
I don't care if my dad gets mad at me.

00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:15.930
I want to wait for Nobou-san.

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:42.860
Abeno-dono, Ashiya-dono!

00:19:43.180 --> 00:19:46.460
Nobou-san! Nobou-san!

00:19:48.930 --> 00:19:53.480
Oh, my. I tripped at the very end.

00:19:53.480 --> 00:19:56.680
I was finally able to leave.

00:19:57.240 --> 00:20:00.750
Because you said you'd wait for me,

00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:04.140
I finally... finally...

00:20:04.900 --> 00:20:09.640
I finally faced my friend 
and was able to say goodbye.

00:20:10.260 --> 00:20:12.340
<i>It must have been far more painful</i>

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:14.980
<i>than either of us imagined.</i>

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:19.150
<i>But we said we'd wait for him, 
so he had faith in us</i>

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:21.530
<i>and made it this far.</i>

00:20:23.430 --> 00:20:25.060
Thank you for coming.

00:20:25.860 --> 00:20:29.160
It must have been hard on your own.

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:34.170
No, thank you for waiting.

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:36.580
The farm...

00:20:41.240 --> 00:20:44.040
Nobou-dono, I've been waiting for you.

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:45.430
Abeno-dono.

00:20:47.240 --> 00:20:51.430
Abeno-dono, allow me to ask you again.

00:20:51.940 --> 00:20:55.510
Will you send me to the Underworld?

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:00.190
Very well.

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:11.240
<i>This is a portal to the Underworld?</i>

00:21:11.860 --> 00:21:13.690
<i>My friend,</i>

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:19.040
<i>I will not forget the days we spent 
together in the mundane world.</i>

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:21.750
<i>I will take all the happiness and pain</i>

00:21:22.320 --> 00:21:25.660
<i>with me to the Underworld.</i>

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:38.940
Thank you for seeing me off!

00:21:40.150 --> 00:21:41.830
Thank you!

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:53.750
Thank you, my friend!

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Next Time "The Purple Sun"</b>

00:23:25.430 --> 00:23:29.020
Zenko's dad definitely has 
the wrong idea about me.

00:23:29.020 --> 00:23:30.700
The blond and handsome Abeno-san

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:34.860
and his bewitching sidelong glances 
seem way more dangerous to me.

00:23:34.860 --> 00:23:36.140
Who are you calling dangerous?

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:38.400
Abeno-san, how long have you been there?!

00:23:38.400 --> 00:23:39.660
Since the beginning.
